---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Metabolic Intelligence · Klere"
  description="Klere positioning: AGI-grade reliability is the hardware and software pair, not the algorithm alone. The metabolic envelope is the physical condition of the best answer, not a cheaper answer. Edge and resource-optimized central. Hyperscale water and power are not required by design. Research owns the claims. Klere builds the hardware. Metabolic Intelligence is the product."
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Product white paper · about · one-pager</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Metabolic Intelligence for Klere
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-brand-white">Why this is the future.</strong> Energy is the binding constraint (Shannon, Landauer, Value of Information).
      The transformer corridor can keep improving and still plateau as a deployment future, because uncapped import is no longer what buys the next useful answer.
      <strong class="text-brand-white">Metabolic Intelligence</strong> is the class in which the envelope is the physical condition of the best answer.
      It is not a Faustian choice and not the cheapest answer.
      It is designed for <strong class="text-brand-white">Klere</strong> (<a href="https://klere.ai" class="text-brand-cyan">klere.ai</a>).
      Research owns the claims. Klere builds the hardware. Metabolic Intelligence is the product.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-brand-white">The pair, not the algorithm.</strong>
      Current fields map AGI to the algorithm. Metabolic Intelligence refuses that split.
      Computers are hardware. Software is applied engineering written for that hardware.
      The interface is a tradeoff among physics, applied mathematics, and materials science.
      AGI-grade reliability is the pair.
      The hardware lottery (Hooker, 2020) is settled: ideas look like progress when they fit available chips.
      Mixture of Limits navigates Lookup, then Formula, then Solver, then Model, because each gear needs a fabric that is available, accessible, and capable.
      <a href="/products/mei/#the-pair-not-the-algorithm" class="text-brand-cyan">The pairing in the paper</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-brand-white">Where it runs.</strong> The <strong class="text-brand-white">edge</strong>
      (coin-cell tags, binding classifiers, metabolic schedules) and the
      <strong class="text-brand-white">resource-optimized central</strong> datacenter
      (budget-capped, grid-following lean campus under OpenADR / DSX Flex).
      Not an uncapped transformer hyperscale campus.
      <strong class="text-brand-white">Mixture of Limits</strong> chooses the gear: Lookup, then Formula, then Solver, then Model.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-brand-white">Every existing fabric.</strong>
      Klere is where Metabolic Intelligence works best. The class is not confined to Klere.
      The same envelope runs on GPU and CUDA stacks, Cortex-M tags, CPU and WASM lookup hosts, and accelerator cards, and on the neuromorphic, analog, and photonic substrates the paper already cites.
      Each host pays an interface tax against Klere-native: data movement, runtime shim, precision, latency, and meter honesty.
      The committed answer is not degraded. Work that would break the envelope is refused or deferred.
      no FPGA board result claimed.
      <a href="/products/mei/#12-state-of-the-art-on-every-existing-compute-fabric" class="text-brand-cyan">Fabric section in the paper</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-brand-white">What a skeptic has to deny.</strong>
      People should not have to fight over energy to eat or to use AI.
      At these envelopes, dedicated water plants, dedicated power plants, and hyperscale cooling loops are
      <strong class="text-brand-white">not required by design</strong>
      (design consequence of microwatt-class tags and the lean-campus pack, not invented liters saved).
      Dismissals and their evidence class are in the paper's objection ledger.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 glass-card p-6 space-y-3" id="investor-one-pager">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Investor / partner one-pager</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Problem.</strong> The default future is transformer scale plus the hyperscale power and water plant that scale presupposes.
        Cold-chain and grid operators need intelligence that fits a stated joule envelope. Energy binds. Uncapped import does not.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Offer.</strong> Klere embodies Metabolic Intelligence as edge and lean central. The envelope is how the best answer is obtained.
        Binding classifiers, physics-informed features, and test-time close make answers reachable that were thought impossible.
        Grid levers and routing refuse or defer work that would violate the envelope. They do not degrade the certified answer. The answer that commits is the best one.
        The <code class="text-brand-cyan">J(m|q)</code> obtain-router prices Lookup → Formula → Solver → Model before spend, and the estimator is capped.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Why not hyperscale water/power.</strong>
        The class targets lower continuous budgets by construction (µW tags; MW-capped lean campus).
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Evidence classes (sell separately).</strong>
        <em>Proven pack:</em> emulator binding classifier vs MLP counts; SmellNet sequential protocol; datasheet+schedule ~10 µW tag model;
        OpenADR 3.1 / DSX Flex protocol demos + scenario table; obtain-router math / ledger bands.
        <em>Roadmap:</em> Klere SKU packaging for tags, lean-campus operator product, gateway DX beyond software reference implementation companions.
        <em>Estimate:</em> Wh/answer curves, CR2032 years, campus plant watts. Labeled until Metered.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">GTM slices.</strong>
        (1) Edge pack: recognition and schedule evidence. Roadmap SKU.
        (2) Lean-campus flexibility: protocol demos and scenario table. Roadmap operator product.
        (3) Obtain stack: router math and software reference implementation companions. Roadmap gateway packaging.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Peer honesty.</strong>
        Logical Intelligence, World Labs / V-JEPA, Dynamo / DSX / AEMA, and neuromorphic MCUs own slices.
        None presently combine tag ↔ lean-campus + OpenADR/DSX + <code class="text-brand-cyan">J(m|q)</code> + binding classifiers as one class.
        Software reference implementation: no FPGA board result claimed.
      </p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-brand-white">Forbidden without meters.</strong>
        Invented liters/gallons saved; Wh/answer as board <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j</code>;
        AEMA latency numbers; Anwar chicken accuracy; “100% served through 90% cut” as a universal field claim.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2" id="companion-laws">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Research behind this product</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        This is a product white paper, kept apart from the research catalog.
        Research papers: <a href="/papers/agency/" class="text-brand-cyan">Thermodynamic Bounds and an Optimal Tempo for Goal-Holding Agents</a> ·
        <a href="/papers/gates/" class="text-brand-cyan">Metered Commit Gates</a> (Notational Intelligence owns the commit; Mixture of Limits chooses the gear) ·
        <a href="/papers/satiation/" class="text-brand-cyan">Task Satiation vs. Aggregate Rebound</a> (the stop).
        Essay: <a href="/papers/spellcheck/" class="text-brand-cyan">Spell Check is Global</a>.
        Other white paper: <a href="/products/jouleos/" class="text-brand-cyan">The Search for JouleOS</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/products/mei/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-dark bg-brand-amber px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-gold transition-colors">
        Read white paper → /products/mei/
      </a>
      <a href="/pdfs/mei.pdf" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-amber border border-brand-amber/40 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-amber/10 transition-colors" download>
        Download PDF
      </a>
      <a href="/living/mei/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-cyan border border-brand-cyan/30 px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:bg-brand-cyan/10 transition-colors">
        Teaching figures
      </a>
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate border border-brand-border px-4 py-2.5 rounded-md no-underline hover:text-brand-white transition-colors">
        ← Catalog
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 glass-card p-6 space-y-3">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Paths</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/products/mei/</span> → white paper prose (glossary + claim ledger in appendices)</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/pdfs/mei.pdf</span> → downloadable white paper PDF</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/living/mei/</span> → teaching figures (Manim + pack charts)</p>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-brand-slate"><span class="text-brand-cyan">/about/mei/</span> → this Klere positioning one-pager</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6 space-y-2">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray">Status and measurement bounds</p>
      <p class="font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        Product white paper, not a journal final. Public klere.ai is thin access framing, not a shipped feature catalog.
        Datasheet + schedule ≠ board package power. Emulator instruction counts ≠ wattmeter.
        Curves / ledger Wh are labeled estimates or measured-kernel models.
        Software reference implementation: <code class="text-brand-cyan">measured_j</code> only when Metered;
        no FPGA board result claimed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
